<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819–1901</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as M. W. Pretorius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> leader, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-pretorius">Andries Pretorius</a>. He was the first president of the South African Republic, from 1857 to 1871, uniting the separate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> communities under the constitution of 1858 and making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> the capital. He was also president of the Orange Free State from 1860 to 1863.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marthinus-wessel-pretorius.jpg" alt="Marthinus Wessel Pretorius" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not recorded · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M_W_Pretorius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
